The step that would break first at 1000× input growth is the streaming aggregation state, especially the keyword counting and windowed volume queries, because Spark must keep growing state for many words and time windows. To fix this, I would use watermarks more carefully, limit the keyword vocabulary, and move from memory sinks to scalable sinks such as Parquet, Delta Lake, or Kafka. I would also repartition the stream so Spark can distribute the work more efficiently across multiple executors.
